WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.949
Film Courage: Well, it’s 2016 (at the taping
of this interview), August 2016.

00:00:02.949 --> 00:00:08.320
A summer day in Los Angeles…[laughs]…I
don’t know why I feel the need to say this…but

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.860
we met with you the first time in 2012.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.210
That was 4 years ago.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:16.699
So since that time, a lot has happened in
your life.

00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:20.269
You’ve been part of many projects, different
things.

00:00:20.269 --> 00:00:27.130
Have you become more idealistic about filmmaking,
less so, more realistic about what is needed

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.130
to work in Hollywood?

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.489
Daniel Stamm: That is a great question.

00:00:29.489 --> 00:00:34.230
Have you talked to people who get more idealistic
as their career goes on?

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.900
I want to talk to those people.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:36.900
Film Courage: [Laughs].

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.820
Daniel Stamm: It’s an interesting question
because after we last met I think I was just

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.830
in preparation for a movie.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:47.110
I think I was about to shoot 13 SINS, my last
feature film.

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:49.550
I haven’t made a feature film since then.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:54.001
And it’s interesting if I’ve gotten more
idealistic or less so.

00:00:54.001 --> 00:01:00.410
I think it’s a mixture of both because I
am very proud of 13 SINS but it never went

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:01.410
anywhere.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.580
It made nine thousand dollars at the box office.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:08.390
It came after THE LAST EXORCISM which was,
you can discuss whether it was a better film

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:13.850
or a worse film or whatever, but box office
wise it was a 70 million dollar success going

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:18.880
to a nine thousand dollar complete failure
at the box office, right?

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.549
Which I would claim I have nothing to do with
either.

00:01:21.549 --> 00:01:25.679
Not with that success or with that failure
because of marketing and how much money is

00:01:25.679 --> 00:01:27.040
being pumped into stuff.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:30.819
THE LAST EXORCISM has a marketing budget of
24 million dollars.

00:01:30.819 --> 00:01:36.030
So it’s easier to get people to see it and
make that kind of money.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:42.130
13 SINS didn’t have a single dollar of marketing
budget and that depended on (without pointing

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:45.090
any fingers) who buys your movie.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:50.660
And in that case the company that bought the
movie just before 13 SINS was going to be

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:56.159
released had a huge flop with a movie that
they had big hopes for and had just done a

00:01:56.159 --> 00:01:57.619
big marketing campaign for.

00:01:57.619 --> 00:02:03.549
They didn’t have the capacity to get 13
SINS released theatrically.

00:02:03.549 --> 00:02:10.119
So suddenly you are a VOD movie, which is
not a problem but it is a difference of if

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:13.180
you see the chart of your career, the way
it’s perceived.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:19.840
You’re going from the world wide theatrical
movie to the VOD movie in America, which means

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.110
nowhere else is it going to go theatrical.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:29.010
So suddenly you have a movie that is basically
disappearing which has nothing to do with

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.840
its quality.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.910
This success did not necessarily have anything
to do with its quality.

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:37.680
But you know you are being held accountable.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:44.400
So I then kind of had to see where to get
the next paycheck from because suddenly I

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:50.220
am not this filmmaker anymore because Hollywood
is…you are worth as much as your last project

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.090
made at the box office basically.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:54.760
So I was worth this much after THE LAST EXORCISM
[gestures up high with his hand] and I was

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.470
worth this much with 13 SINS [gestures down
low with his hands].

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:00.290
It’s a real problem to get yourself out
of.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.810
So the answer is TV.

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:03.810
And I was always like “I don’t want to
do TV.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.319
I don’t want to do TV.”

00:03:05.319 --> 00:03:11.819
But I had to get my rent check from somewhere
and I think the landscape really changed.

00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:16.420
Maybe I’m just telling myself that because
I’m doing TV but I think a lot has happened

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:21.959
since we last spoke in terms of with TRUE
DETECTIVE, with GAME OF THRONES, that some

00:03:21.959 --> 00:03:25.579
of the best storytelling today is being done
in TV.

00:03:25.579 --> 00:03:30.469
So it’s not actually as bleak a world has
I would have thought back then….QUESTION

00:03:30.469 --> 00:03:31.469
FOR THE VIEWERS: How much blame should be
on a director if their movie bombs at the

00:03:31.469 --> 00:03:31.969
box office?

